    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46231" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub-vŏlo</span></b> , āre,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to fly up</i> or <i>upwards</i> (rare
			but class.): hae (partes corporum) sursum in caelestem
			locum subvo lent, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 17, 40</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">avis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 790</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex agmine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 507</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praepes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 577</span></i>
			: ad capita, Aug. Civ. Dei, 18, 16 <i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
						Vict. Vir. Ill. 6, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
